Address Independent Round 2 CHANGES_REQUIRED verdict:

1. Dynamic port allocation (Finding 2):
   - Added Get-AvailableLoopbackPort() helper using port 0 OS binding
   - Replaced hardcoded ports 29114/29115/29117/29118 with runtime allocation
   - Tests 15a-15c now use fully dynamic isolated ports

2. Strict Agent Scan metadata parsing (Finding 3):
   - Require exactly one Name: field matching "snyk-agent-scan"
   - Require exactly one Version: field with complete format (no trailing text)
   - Added Tests 19a-19d for malformed metadata (trailing garbage, duplicates, wrong name)

3. Behavioral test fixtures (Finding 4):
   - Enhanced Test 17 (Promptfoo) with controlled npm JSON fixture
   - Fixed Test 18 to use realistic non-zero exit code for missing pip
   - Enhanced Test 20 to place Python/npm fixtures in spaced paths
   - Enhanced Test 21 (Renovate) to prove npm metadata wins over noisy CLI

4. Review evidence (Finding 5):
   - Updated Codex review record with Round 1 commit bcc9094
   - Documented Round 2 findings and resolutions
   - Updated test count to 25 (added 4 strict parsing tests)

All 25 ecosystem tests pass. Format check ready for CI verification.

